# Docker build context excludes (review §12). The x86 sim build uses the REPO ROOT as its build
# context (docker/docker_build_x86_sim.sh: context = "$SCRIPT_DIR/.."), so without this it ships
# every weight, log, and run artifact to the daemon for a Dockerfile that COPYs nothing.
#
# IMPORTANT: the ros2 sidecar Dockerfiles DO `COPY src/unitree_sdk2_python` and `COPY ros2_ws`
# (docker/Dockerfile_ros2_sidecar*), so those two paths are deliberately NOT excluded here.

# Large model weights (mounted at runtime, never COPYed)
weights/
*.pt
*.trt
*.onnx
*.engine

# Runtime logs, traces, and per-run artifacts
log/
logs/
run_logs/
debug_logs/
tmp/

# perf_tracker generated data (volatile; not build input)
src/perf_tracker/data/

# Git metadata and Python caches
.git/
.github/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# Editor / OS cruft
*.tmp
.env
